      "normalized_sha256": "c81ca83083d7457acd8bc03869be055c6f82860af5fcb6ab0df7413577ec1931",
      "rationale": "This is the base equation of the scanHappy structural recurrence: an empty remaining character sequence contributes true. It defines the summary value, matches no execution configuration, and adds no independent mathematical fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-c81ca83083d7457acd8bc03869be055c6f82860af5fcb6ab0df7413577ec1931",
      "start_line": 9,
      "text": "  rule scanHappy(.IntSeq, _:Int, _:Int, _:Int) => true"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 12,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "424ad9bede59bccdcf23851333637603f57a311d80fcb5fef99140e39aae7991",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded warm-up equation of scanHappy for I < 2. It defines how the summary consumes one character and advances its two-character history before complete three-character windows exist; recursion is structural on REST.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-424ad9bede59bccdcf23851333637603f57a311d80fcb5fef99140e39aae7991",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule scanHappy(iCons(C:Int, REST:IntSeq), I:Int, _:Int, P1:Int)\n    => scanHappy(REST, I +Int 1, P1, C)\n    requires I <Int 2"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 18,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "738ed76d501e1fe77a5aa4c3808cc7f2254b9f6b94e6b2a6378b84afed317e55",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded steady-state equation of scanHappy for I >= 2. It defines the summary by conjoining the three pairwise code inequalities for the current window and recurring structurally on REST, rather than asserting a separate domain fact or rewriting program execution.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-738ed76d501e1fe77a5aa4c3808cc7f2254b9f6b94e6b2a6378b84afed317e55",
      "start_line": 13,
      "text": "  rule scanHappy(iCons(C:Int, REST:IntSeq), I:Int, P2:Int, P1:Int)\n    => (C =/=Int P1)\n       andBool (C =/=Int P2)\n       andBool (P1 =/=Int P2)\n       andBool scanHappy(REST, I +Int 1, P1, C)\n    requires I >=Int 2"
    }
  ],
